# Keep the build context small + leak-free. The Dockerfile only needs
# requirements.txt + app/ (the model is trained inside the builder stage).
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.pytest_cache/
**/.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
models/
# ...except the Safety-NLP manifest: the governance record that pins the model
# revisions + hashes the monolith image downloads at build time.
!models/safety/manifest.json
mlruns/
monitoring/
data/
# ...except the reviewed GoWhere opening-hours snapshot, which is RUNTIME data,
# not a build artifact. `data/` excluded it from the context entirely, so
# gpgowhere.SNAPSHOT_PATH did not exist in the image and profiles() returned []
# — silently disabling the closed-clinic filter, i.e. the container could route
# a patient to a shut clinic. (The .npz training snapshot stays excluded: it is
# 6000 synthetic rows the runtime never reads.)
!data/gpgowhere_hours.json
tests/
.env
.env.*
*.md
requirements-dev.txt
requirements-mlops.txt
